<title>MEXICO: GBM Atlantico to issue $25 million debt.</title>
<headline>GBM Atlantico to issue $25 million debt.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican financial group GBM Atlantico SA de CV said it would carry out a public offering of six-year mandatorily convertible subordinated obligations worth $25 million on Thursday.</p>
<p>In a statement released via the Mexican Stock Exchange, GBM Atlantico said the obligations would be convertible into A, B and L shares in the company.</p>
<p>The company said it would issue 25,000 of the titles, each worth a nominal $1,000, paying 9.75 percent interest. Interest would be payable on a quarterly basis.</p>
<p>Mexican brokerage Accival would lead the issue, it added.</p>
<p>((--Martin Langfield, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9558))</p>
